---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
// Converted from the OKAD case artifact. Styles are scoped under .case-designed.
const title = "Their ads explained the feature. Ours show what happens next. | OKAD Agency";
const description = "Lookalikey puts anyone's face on a birthday card. Its ads showed how that works. We built a creator batch around the moment after: the family chat explodes, the card stays on the fridge, it becomes someone's wallpaper.";
const ogImage = "/images/cases/lookalikey-ugc-ads/img-01.jpg";
---

<Base title={title} description={description} ogImage={ogImage}>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Instrument+Serif:ital@0;1&family=Reenie+Beanie&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="case-designed">






<!-- COVER -->
<section class="cover">
  <div class="w">
    <div class="cover-grid">
      <div class="stack" style="gap:24px">
        <span class="kick">Personalised face-swap cards · DTC · UK and US</span>
        <h1>Their ads explained the feature. <span class="cap g">Ours show what happens next.</span></h1>
        <p class="lead">Lookalikey puts anyone's face on a birthday card. Its ads showed how that works. We built a creator batch around the moment after: the family chat explodes, the card stays on the fridge, it becomes someone's wallpaper.</p>
        <div class="meta">
          <div><b>April–May 2026</b><span>From concepts to delivery</span></div>
          <div><b>3 UGC creators</b><span>Three stories each, 9:16</span></div>
          <div><b>Our scope</b><span>Ad research, concepts, scripts, casting, shooting briefs, chat mockups, editing</span></div>
          <div><b>Not our scope</b><span>Media buying: the client runs the ads</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="collage" aria-label="Frames from the ads">
        <div class="ann hand" style="right:-6px;top:-74px">real frames from the ads<svg width="70" height="60" viewBox="0 0 70 60"><path d="M6 6 C 34 2, 56 18, 60 52"/><path d="M51 44 L60 54 L66 42"/></svg></div>
        <figure class="ph"><img alt="Creator with laptop: I used to forget every birthday" src="/images/cases/lookalikey-ugc-ads/img-01.jpg" loading="lazy"></figure>
        <figure class="ph"><img alt="Creator holding a dragon card" src="/images/cases/lookalikey-ugc-ads/img-02.jpg" loading="lazy"></figure>
        <figure class="ph"><img alt="Face-swap card set as phone wallpaper" src="/images/cases/lookalikey-ugc-ads/img-03.jpg" loading="lazy"></figure>
        <figure class="ph"><img alt="Card on the fridge for 4 months" src="/images/cases/lookalikey-ugc-ads/img-04.jpg" loading="lazy"></figure>
        <figure class="ph"><img alt="Creator: I made one card" src="/images/cases/lookalikey-ugc-ads/img-05.jpg" loading="lazy"></figure>
        <figure class="ph"><img alt="Stack of printed face-swap cards" src="/images/cases/lookalikey-ugc-ads/img-06.jpg" loading="lazy"></figure>
        <figure class="ph"><img alt="Creator: I used to forget every birthday" src="/images/cases/lookalikey-ugc-ads/img-07.jpg" loading="lazy"></figure>
        <figure class="ph"><img alt="Creator fanning out cards: lookalikey.com" src="/images/cases/lookalikey-ugc-ads/img-08.jpg" loading="lazy"></figure>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="strip">
      <div><b>9</b><span>UGC videos delivered</span></div>
      <div><b>3</b><span>creators, each with her own scripts</span></div>
      <div><b>14</b><span>concepts pitched: 7 video, 7 static</span></div>
      <div><b>0</b><span>times the word "AI" is said on camera</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="howto"><span><b>Hook</b> = the first seconds that make people stop scrolling.</span><span><b>B-roll</b> = footage that plays under the voice.</span><span><b>Face swap</b> = the customer's photo placed onto a card design.</span></div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Q1 -->
<section>
  <div class="w two">
    <div class="stack">
      <span class="q-kick">Q1 · Why not keep the ads they had?</span>
      <h2>Because "one click" <span class="cap p">doesn't make anyone laugh.</span></h2>
      <p class="lead">The brand's live ads led with the mechanism: "one click and their face is added". Competitors sold jokes or step-by-step demos. Nobody showed the part people actually buy the card for: the reaction when it lands.</p>
      <p class="pro"><b>For marketers</b>Meta Ad Library audit of the brand and two competitors. Rule we applied: if a hook says how the product works, rewrite it as what someone feels.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="before-after">
      <div class="box before">
        <span class="tag">What we got</span>
        <ul>
          <li>Live ads built on the feature</li>
          <li>Digital e-cards and printed cards</li>
          <li>Different offers in the UK and US</li>
          <li>Customers who keep and frame cards</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="box dark">
        <span class="tag g">The brief</span>
        <ul>
          <li>Hooks about the moment, not the tech</li>
          <li>A real printed card on camera</li>
          <li>Push the 3-for bundle offer</li>
          <li>"Face swap" only, never "AI"</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Q2 -->
<section>
  <div class="w">
    <div class="stack">
      <span class="q-kick">Q2 · Where did the stories come from?</span>
      <h2>Seven ideas, <span class="cap g">and the client's notes on each.</span></h2>
      <p class="lead">We pitched 7 video and 7 static concepts as hooks and visual direction only, before writing a single script. The founder's comments on the pitch turned into plot points.</p>
      <p class="pro"><b>For marketers</b>Every concept came with a source map: what we took from the client's ads, what from competitors and what was new. Empty territory we found: reactions, keepsakes, pets and wall art.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="sources">
      <div class="box"><span class="tag g">1 · We audit</span><h3>What everyone already runs</h3><p>Brand and competitor ads, hook by hook: features, jokes, tutorials. Then what nobody shows.</p></div>
      <div class="box"><span class="tag g">2 · We pitch</span><h3>Concepts before scripts</h3><p>Seven video ideas with four hooks each, plus seven statics. Cheap to change, fast to approve.</p></div>
      <div class="box"><span class="tag g">3 · We merge</span><h3>Client notes into the plot</h3><p>The founder knows what customers do with the cards. That knowledge went straight into the scripts.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="insights">
      <div class="ins">
        <div class="quote">"Can we position it around a physical card rather than digital?"<small>CLIENT NOTE ON THE GROUP-CHAT IDEA</small></div>
        <div class="arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg width="64" height="24" viewBox="0 0 64 24"><path d="M3 14 C 20 9, 40 16, 58 11"/><path d="M50 4 L59 11 L50 18"/></svg></div>
        <figure class="ph"><img alt="Creator showing the printed dragon card" src="/images/cases/lookalikey-ugc-ads/img-02.jpg" loading="lazy"></figure>
        <p><b>The card arrives first, then the chat explodes.</b> She photographs the printed card on the kitchen table, sends it to the family, and five more orders follow that week.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ins dark">
        <div class="quote">"Many customers keep their cards. Some have framed them."<small>CLIENT NOTE ON THE FRIDGE IDEA</small></div>
        <div class="arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg width="64" height="24" viewBox="0 0 64 24"><path d="M3 14 C 20 9, 40 16, 58 11"/><path d="M50 4 L59 11 L50 18"/></svg></div>
        <figure class="ph"><img alt="Card on the fridge for 4 months" src="/images/cases/lookalikey-ugc-ads/img-04.jpg" loading="lazy"></figure>
        <p><b>Became The Fridge Test.</b> The one card that survived among the kids' drawings, a neighbour who asked if it was a painting, and a friend who framed hers.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ins">
        <div class="quote">"It may encourage bulk purchases."<small>CLIENT NOTE ON THE BIRTHDAY HACK</small></div>
        <div class="arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg width="64" height="24" viewBox="0 0 64 24"><path d="M3 14 C 20 9, 40 16, 58 11"/><path d="M50 4 L59 11 L50 18"/></svg></div>
        <figure class="ph"><img alt="Creator: I made 12 birthday cards in one night" src="/images/cases/lookalikey-ugc-ads/img-09.jpg" loading="lazy"></figure>
        <p><b>Twelve cards in one evening, on the 3-for offer.</b> A stack ordered home for the year, and cards posted straight to relatives who live far away.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Q3 -->
<section>
  <div class="w">
    <div class="stack">
      <span class="q-kick">Q3 · Why nine videos?</span>
      <h2>Three creators, three stories, <span class="cap g">never the same script.</span></h2>
      <p class="lead">Each creator told each story her own way: a different hook, a different relative, different details. The test shows which story sells and which voice tells it best, without nine copies of one video.</p>
      <p class="pro"><b>For marketers</b>Four story types across nine videos: group chat (social proof), fridge (keepsake), wallpaper (daily visibility), birthday hack (bundle and planning).</p>
    </div>
    <details class="more"><summary>See the nine hooks</summary>
    <div class="mx-wrap">
      <table class="mx">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Creator</th><th scope="col">Story</th><th scope="col">Hook</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Andrea</td><td>Fridge Test</td><td class="h">"This card has been on my fridge for 4 months. Every other card went in the bin."</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Andrea</td><td>Birthday Hack</td><td class="h">"I made 12 birthday cards in one night. I'm set for the entire year."</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Andrea</td><td>Group Chat</td><td class="h">"I sent this to the family group chat. Now everyone wants one."</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Jenny</td><td>Group Chat</td><td class="h">"I made one card. Now my whole family's obsessed."</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Jenny</td><td>Wallpaper</td><td class="h">"Everyone who sees my phone asks about this wallpaper."</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Jenny</td><td>Birthday Hack</td><td class="h">"I used to forget every birthday. Now I'm the most organised person in my family."</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Charity</td><td>Group Chat</td><td class="h">"I accidentally became the family gift hero."</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Charity</td><td>Wallpaper</td><td class="h">"The only wallpaper that survived my phone clear-out."</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Charity</td><td>Birthday Hack</td><td class="h">"I used to forget every birthday. Now I'm the most organised person."</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    </details>
    <div class="chips">
      <span class="chip"><b>7 + 7</b> concepts pitched</span>
      <span class="chip"><b>4</b> hooks per video concept</span>
      <span class="chip"><b>4</b> stories filmed</span>
      <span class="chip"><b>3</b> personas</span>
      <span class="chip"><b>1</b> shooting brief per creator</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Q4 CASTING -->
<section class="dew">
  <div class="w">
    <div class="stack">
      <span class="q-kick">Q4 · Who tells the stories?</span>
      <h2>Three women, <span class="cap g">three kinds of family.</span></h2>
      <p class="lead">The buyer is usually the person who remembers everyone's birthday, or wishes she did. We cast three versions of her and gave each a tone in the brief, not just lines.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cast three">
      <div class="person">
        <figure class="ph"><img alt="Jenny" src="/images/cases/lookalikey-ugc-ads/img-05.jpg" loading="lazy"></figure>
        <div class="stack" style="gap:6px"><span class="kick">Grandmother energy</span><h3>Jenny</h3><ul><li>"If a 58-year-old nan can do this…"</li><li>Granddaughter's card on the coffee table</li><li>Family chat: "Do Grandad!"</li></ul></div>
      </div>
      <div class="person">
        <figure class="ph"><img alt="Andrea" src="/images/cases/lookalikey-ugc-ads/img-10.jpg" loading="lazy"></figure>
        <div class="stack" style="gap:6px"><span class="kick">Warm mum</span><h3>Andrea</h3><ul><li>Fridge full of kids' drawings</li><li>12 cards with a cup of tea</li><li>Nephew Zac's dragon card</li></ul></div>
      </div>
      <div class="person">
        <figure class="ph"><img alt="Charity" src="/images/cases/lookalikey-ugc-ads/img-11.jpg" loading="lazy"></figure>
        <div class="stack" style="gap:6px"><span class="kick">The friend with recommendations</span><h3>Charity</h3><ul><li>Wallpaper that survived the clear-out</li><li>Five cards in one week</li><li>Niece far away gets hers instantly</li></ul></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Q5 PRODUCTION -->
<section>
  <div class="w">
    <div class="stack">
      <span class="q-kick">Q5 · How do you film a reaction on cue?</span>
      <h2>We designed the group chat <span class="cap y">before the shoot.</span></h2>
      <p class="lead">Reactions sell this product, but a real family won't reply on cue. We made the chat screens ourselves and sent them to creators to show on camera, together with a shot list for each of them.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="rule-row">
      <div class="box"><span class="tag">Shared b-roll</span><h3>Same for every creator</h3><p>Browsing the site, picking a design, the face appearing, the cart with pricing, the group-chat screen.</p></div>
      <div class="box"><span class="tag">Per creator</span><h3>Shots for her story</h3><p>The fridge walk, an unboxing, a fanned stack of cards; or the lock screen and an unlock for the wallpaper story.</p></div>
      <div class="box"><span class="tag">Brief</span><h3>Light, sound, tone</h3><p>Daylight, a mic, bright clothes, eyes on the lens. Plus a tone line: "nan", "warm mum", "friend with the best tips".</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="hn" style="justify-content:flex-end;margin-top:14px"><svg style="transform:scaleX(-1)" width="60" height="46" viewBox="0 0 60 46"><path d="M4 42 C 26 42, 34 10, 54 6"/><path d="M45 1 L55 6 L47 13"/></svg><span class="hand">the chat is ours, the laughs are theirs</span></div>
    <div class="reel">
      <figure class="ph"><img alt="Designed family chat" src="/images/cases/lookalikey-ugc-ads/img-12.jpg" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Chat screen we designed</figcaption></figure>
      <figure class="ph"><img alt="Chat overlay in the video" src="/images/cases/lookalikey-ugc-ads/img-13.jpg" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Shown inside the story</figcaption></figure>
      <figure class="ph"><img alt="Lookalikey site" src="/images/cases/lookalikey-ugc-ads/img-14.jpg" loading="lazy"><figcaption>The real site flow</figcaption></figure>
      <figure class="ph"><img alt="Card as wallpaper" src="/images/cases/lookalikey-ugc-ads/img-03.jpg" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Lock screen b-roll</figcaption></figure>
      <figure class="ph"><img alt="Printed cards" src="/images/cases/lookalikey-ugc-ads/img-06.jpg" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Printed cards in hand</figcaption></figure>
      <figure class="ph"><img alt="Card on the fridge" src="/images/cases/lookalikey-ugc-ads/img-15.jpg" loading="lazy"><figcaption>The card that stayed</figcaption></figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Q6 BEATS -->
<section class="dew">
  <div class="w two">
    <div class="stack">
      <span class="q-kick">Q6 · What does every story hit?</span>
      <h2>Five beats, <span class="cap g">from guilt to hero.</span></h2>
      <p class="lead">Every script starts with a small, familiar failure and ends with the creator as the thoughtful one in the family. The product sits in the middle, as the reason things changed.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="stack">
      <div class="hooks">
        <div class="box dark"><span class="tag g dewtag">Details we wrote in</span>
          <ul class="hook-list">
            <li>A "Sorry for your loss" card with "Happy Birthday" in pen</li>
            <li>Up since Christmas among the kids' drawings</li>
            <li>Survived two phone updates and a storage-full panic</li>
            <li>"Mum, when did you become so thoughtful?"</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="box plain"><span class="tag">Checked against the site</span>
          <ul class="hook-list">
            <li>Real order: design first, then photo</li>
            <li>Right offer per market: £10 or $12</li>
            <li>Delivery that exists in that country</li>
            <li>"Face swap", never "AI"</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="w">
    <div class="timeline" aria-label="Story structure">
      <div><span class="s">beat 1</span><b>The failure</b><span class="q">"I'd remember the morning of and grab whatever was left on the shelf."</span></div>
      <div><span class="s">beat 2</span><b>The discovery</b><span class="q">"My friend told me about this website where you swap someone's face onto a card."</span></div>
      <div><span class="s">beat 3</span><b>The moment</b><span class="q">"'Mum, can you make one for Uncle Steve?'"</span></div>
      <div><span class="s">beat 4</span><b>The proof</b><span class="q">"This card has been on my fridge for 4 months."</span></div>
      <div><span class="s">beat 5</span><b>Name + nudge</b><span class="q">"It's called Lookalikey. You're welcome."</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Q7 RESULTS -->
<section>
  <div class="w">
    <div class="stack">
      <span class="q-kick">Q7 · What did the client get?</span>
      <h2>Nine videos, <span class="cap g">four stories, three voices.</span></h2>
      <p class="lead">A batch where every story is told by more than one person, so the brand learns both what to say and who should say it. Plus a bank of approved concepts for the next rounds.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="kpis">
      <div class="kpi"><b>9</b><span>UGC videos, 9:16, three creators with three stories each.</span></div>
      <div class="kpi"><b>4</b><span>stories tested: group chat, fridge, wallpaper and birthday hack.</span></div>
      <div class="kpi"><b>14</b><span>concepts with hooks, including statics, ready for the next batch.</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="hn" style="justify-content:flex-end;margin-top:14px"><svg style="transform:scaleX(-1)" width="60" height="46" viewBox="0 0 60 46"><path d="M4 42 C 26 42, 34 10, 54 6"/><path d="M45 1 L55 6 L47 13"/></svg><span class="hand">each story, more than one voice</span></div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- OFFER -->
<section>
  <div class="w">
    <div class="offer">
      <span class="q-kick">Q8 · What would this look like for you?</span>
      <h2>Your ads explain the product. <span class="cap g">We find the moment people share.</span></h2>
      <p class="lead">For gifting and personalised-product brands whose ads show how it works, but not why anyone would send it.</p>
      <div class="steps">
        <div class="step"><span class="mono">step 1</span><b>Audit</b><p>Your ads and competitors', hook by hook.</p></div>
        <div class="step"><span class="mono">step 2</span><b>Concepts</b><p>Ideas and hooks first, approved before scripts.</p></div>
        <div class="step"><span class="mono">step 3</span><b>Casting</b><p>Creators who look like your real buyers.</p></div>
        <div class="step"><span class="mono">step 4</span><b>Briefs</b><p>A script and shot list per creator, props included.</p></div>
        <div class="step"><span class="mono">step 5</span><b>Edit</b><p>Every story in several voices, ready to test.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="cta"><a class="btn" href="https://okad.agency" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Book a call · okad.agency</a><span class="hn"><span style="flex:none"><svg width="54" height="22" viewBox="0 0 54 22"><path d="M51 12 C 36 16, 20 7, 5 11"/><path d="M13 4 L4 11 L12 18"/></svg></span><span class="hand">start here</span></span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<footer class="w">OKAD · Lisbon · Client notes and hooks are quoted from the approved concept document and shooting briefs, 2026.</footer>

  </div>
</Base>

<style is:global>
.case-designed{margin:0;padding:0;background:#ffffff}
.case-designed img{max-width:100%}
.case-designed{box-sizing:border-box;padding-top:env(safe-area-inset-top,0px);padding-bottom:env(safe-area-inset-bottom,0px)}.case-designed{scroll-padding-top:env(safe-area-inset-top,0px)}

/* OKAD house style: white page, Instrument Serif caps for headlines, Instrument Sans for reading,
   Reenie Beanie for hand-written notes with drawn arrows. Pastel outline marks the key words;
   dew-green bands and black cards create rhythm. */
.case-designed{
  --paper:#ffffff; --card:#f4f4f1; --ink:#111111; --soft:#5f5f5b; --rule:#e6e6e1;
  --dew:#eefb6e; --dew-ink:#111111; --on-dew-card:#ffffff;
  --yel:#f2fa5a; --mint:#b5f5c6; --lav:#d4d4fc; --peach:#ffe2ad; --lilac:#ecc8fa;
  --hi:var(--dew); --hi-ink:#111111; --pink:#111111;
  --c1:#8f4fd6; --c2:#17904f;
  --stage:#121114; --stage-ink:#f4f4f0; --stage-soft:#b9b9b3;
  --good:#17904f; --mid:#c98a14; --bad:#d03e3e;
  --display:"Instrument Serif","Times New Roman",serif;
  --body:"Instrument Sans","Helvetica Neue",Arial,sans-serif;
  --hand:"Reenie Beanie","Bradley Hand",cursive;
  --mono:var(--body);
  --r:28px;
}
.case-designed{color-scheme:light}

.case-designed *{box-sizing:border-box}
.case-designed{background:var(--paper);color:var(--ink);font-family:var(--body);font-size:17px;line-height:1.55;margin:0}
.case-designed .w{max-width:1180px;margin:0 auto;padding-inline:20px}
.case-designed section{padding-block:96px;position:relative}
.case-designed p{margin:0;max-width:64ch}
.case-designed h1,.case-designed h2{font-family:var(--display);font-weight:400;margin:0;line-height:.94;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:-.012em;text-wrap:balance}
.case-designed h1{font-size:clamp(2.8rem,6.4vw,5.6rem)}
.case-designed h2{font-size:clamp(2.3rem,4.9vw,4.1rem)}
.case-designed h3{font-family:var(--body);font-style:italic;font-weight:600;font-size:1.16rem;line-height:1.2;margin:0;letter-spacing:-.005em}
.case-designed .kick{font-family:var(--body);font-size:.92rem;color:var(--soft)}
.case-designed .lead{font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--soft);max-width:60ch}
.case-designed .stack{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:20px}
.case-designed .mono{font-family:var(--body);font-size:.8rem}
.case-designed .q-kick{font-family:var(--body);font-style:normal;font-weight:400;font-size:1rem;color:var(--soft)}
.case-designed .pro{font-size:.92rem;color:var(--soft);background:var(--card);border-radius:18px;padding:14px 18px 16px;max-width:70ch}
.case-designed .dew .pro{background:rgba(255,255,255,.55)}
.case-designed .pro b{display:block;font-family:var(--hand);font-style:normal;font-weight:400;font-size:1.7rem;line-height:.9;color:var(--ink);margin-bottom:2px}
.case-designed details.more{margin-top:32px}
.case-designed details.more summary{cursor:pointer;font-family:var(--body);font-weight:600;list-style:none;display:inline-flex;gap:10px;align-items:center;padding:12px 20px;border-radius:99px;background:var(--ink);color:var(--paper)}
.case-designed details.more summary::-webkit-details-marker{display:none}
.case-designed details.more summary::after{content:"+"}
.case-designed details.more[open] summary::after{content:"–"}
.case-designed .howto{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px 22px;margin-top:26px;font-size:.88rem;color:var(--soft)}
.case-designed .howto b{color:var(--ink);font-style:normal;font-weight:600}

/* key words: thick pastel outline traced around the letters */
.case-designed .cap{--hl:transparent;color:inherit}
